From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:37:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201: use the gs101 fallbacks
 for the PMU and watchdogs

gs201's PMU, its interrupt generator and the cluster watchdogs are
gs101's, and the bindings now document them with gs101 fallbacks. Use
those, so the nodes validate and the drivers need no gs201 entries.

The PMU also loses "syscon", as on gs101. Its registers are written
through the EL3 monitor, and exynos-pmu registers that regmap with
syscon at probe. With "syscon" in the node, a consumer that looked the
PMU up first (the UFS and USB PHYs and the watchdogs use
syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle()) would get a plain MMIO regmap
whose writes the PMU ignores, and exynos-pmu's own registration would
then fail. The watchdogs are the sharp case: ABL leaves them running,
and if their PMU mask writes were ignored the phone would reset about a
minute after boot. Without "syscon" an early consumer defers until
exynos-pmu has probed. On the boots so far exynos-pmu came first (only
its regmaps exist), so this removes an ordering dependency rather than
fixing a seen failure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi
index 81504af41..5ccb5bd5d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi
@@ -934,7 +934,7 @@ mct: timer@10050000 {
 		 * them at probe unless tmr_atboot is set.
 		 */
 		watchdog_cl0: watchdog@10060000 {
-			compatible = "google,gs201-wdt";
+			compatible = "google,gs201-wdt", "google,gs101-wdt";
 			reg = <0x10060000 0x100>;
 			clocks = <&cmu_misc CLK_GOUT_MISC_WDT_CLUSTER0_PCLK>,
 				 <&oscclk>;
@@ -945,7 +945,7 @@ watchdog_cl0: watchdog@10060000 {
 		};
 
 		watchdog_cl1: watchdog@10070000 {
-			compatible = "google,gs201-wdt";
+			compatible = "google,gs201-wdt", "google,gs101-wdt";
 			reg = <0x10070000 0x100>;
 			clocks = <&cmu_misc CLK_GOUT_MISC_WDT_CLUSTER1_PCLK>,
 				 <&oscclk>;
@@ -974,7 +974,7 @@ sysreg_apm: syscon@18020000 {
 		};
 
 		pmu_system_controller: system-controller@18060000 {
-			compatible = "google,gs201-pmu", "syscon";
+			compatible = "google,gs201-pmu", "google,gs101-pmu";
 			reg = <0x18060000 0x10000>;
 			google,pmu-intr-gen-syscon = <&pmu_intr_gen>;
 
@@ -995,7 +995,8 @@ reboot-mode {
 		};
 
 		pmu_intr_gen: syscon@18070000 {
-			compatible = "google,gs201-pmu-intr-gen", "syscon";
+			compatible = "google,gs201-pmu-intr-gen", "google,gs101-pmu-intr-gen",
+				     "syscon";
 			reg = <0x18070000 0x10000>;
 		};
 
